now how flood warnings are in effect  this morning for areas along nearly the  entire Mississippi River as heavy rain  continues to hit the Mississippi Valley  Jericka Duncan is in Davenport Iowa  where a temporary levee failed sending a  wall of water into downtown streets  jurika good morning good morning this  part of downtown Davenport is pretty  much butted right up against the  Mississippi River and you can tell just  how serious this flooding is by looking  at those cars that are under water  behind me but take a look at this drone  video where you can really see clearly  that when the temporary levee holding  back the Mississippi River breached  yesterday streets and several businesses  downtown were submerged in a matter of  minutes  now the levee had been holding back  rising floodwaters for more than a month  officials urged people to evacuate  immediately but some could not get out  in time emergency responders had to  rescue people from the rooftops of  buildings by boat thankfully as of right  now there are no reported injuries crews  and volunteers scrambled to fill  sandbags and barriers while shop owners  tried salvaging whatever they could a  University of Iowa study finds that  every single County in the state of Iowa  has declared multiple flood related  disasters in the past 30 years even one  County reporting as many as 17 now heavy  rain is expected later today and that  river is expected to crest tonight  possibly just shy of the record which is  twenty two point six feet boy somebody  forgot to tell Mother Nature it's the  first day of May supposed to be sunshine  and lollipops thank you very much
 

